# Frontend Conventions

## Stack

- Next.js 16 App Router, React 19, TypeScript strict, Tailwind CSS 4
- Icons: `lucide-react`. Images: `next/image`.
- State: React hooks only (no external state library)
- Styling: Tailwind utility classes + CSS variables from `globals.css`

## Patterns

- All components use `"use client"` when they need interactivity
- Path alias: `@/*` maps to `frontend/*`
- Utility: `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` for conditional class merging (clsx + tailwind-merge)
- API layer in `@/lib/api.ts` — transforms Rust responses into typed frontend models

## Component Structure

- `app/markets/page.tsx` — main markets page, owns view toggle (card/row)
- `components/EventTable.tsx` — switches between `EventCard` (grid) and `EventRow` (table)
- `components/EventCard.tsx` — card view with per-platform sections
- `components/EventRow.tsx` — table row view with price cells

## Style Guidelines

- Dark mode support via `dark:` variants throughout
- Tabular numbers (`tabular-nums`) for all price displays
- Platform logos: use PNG versions with `next/image`, Polymarket gets `rounded-full`, Kalshi gets `rounded`
- Consistent yes/no indicators: green for YES, red for NO
